From: Tiger Kaovilai <passawit.kaovilai@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] feat(posix): relay paths (--path NAME@HOST:PORT)

A client path can now go through a UDP relay instead of straight to the
server: --path / Path = NAME@HOST:PORT opens a path whose socket is not
pinned to an interface and whose datagrams go to HOST:PORT. What the
relay sends back is handed to the core as if it came from the server
(the address the core last sent to on that path); anything else on the
socket is dropped. NAME labels the path in logs and status.

Use: a device without its own uplink to the server lends one, e.g. a
phone on the LAN sharing its cellular data. QUIC multipath sees the path
from the relay's public address, like any NAT rebinding.

- mqvpn_bind_posix_path_set_relay(ctx, addr, len): the bind side.
- platform/path_spec.h: the NAME@HOST:PORT parser (numeric IPv4 or
  [IPv6]), used when the POSIX platforms create their path slots.
- Linux: relay slots skip the interface pin and the interface/route gates
  of re-add and reactivation (there is no interface to gate on).
- tests/test_bind_posix_socket.c: spec parsing, and a relay path over
  loopback sockets (sends reach the relay, the relay's reply is delivered
  as the server's, a stranger's is dropped).

Signed-off-by: Tiger Kaovilai <passawit.kaovilai@gmail.com>
---
diff -ruN a/include/mqvpn_bind_posix.h b/include/mqvpn_bind_posix.h
--- a/include/mqvpn_bind_posix.h	2026-11-03 14:34:59.828057215 -0500
+++ b/include/mqvpn_bind_posix.h	2026-11-03 16:26:44.959967363 -0500
@@ -82,6 +82,14 @@
 /* Destructor for a ctx the library never took ownership of (add_path failed).
  * Identical to ops.release; never closes the fd. */
 MQVPN_API void mqvpn_bind_posix_path_free(void *ctx);
+/* Make ctx a relay path: every datagram goes to relay (a UDP relay that
+ * forwards it to the server) instead of the peer the core names, and
+ * datagrams received from relay are delivered as if they came from that
+ * peer (the address the core last sent to); anything else arriving on the
+ * socket is dropped. Call before add_path. MQVPN_OK, or
+ * MQVPN_ERR_INVALID_ARG (NULL ctx/relay, not AF_INET/AF_INET6, bad length). */
+MQVPN_API int mqvpn_bind_posix_path_set_relay(void *ctx, const struct sockaddr *relay,
+                                              socklen_t relay_len);
 
 MQVPN_API int mqvpn_bind_posix_path_gro_enabled(const void *ctx); /* 0/1 */
 /* errno of a failed enable, else 0 */
